<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Encryption is not allowed in Amateur radio. OpenGD77 is a firmware for Amateur radio operator, so encryption of any type will not be support.</div></blockquote>I have read this explanation too. A few local repeaters owners allow their close friends to use encryption on their ham repeaters. But while that is the official answer, I wonder if the real explanation is “to modify the FW to do everything it does, encryption had to go to make space for the new features”. GARY.</div></blockquote>As I understand it, OpenGD77 will have a legal problem once it is not purely for amateur radio, hence, the dev team is trying to avoid anything that can be view as non-ham. However, that is my understanding. We might need to wait for the dev team to say on this one.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Mon Apr 07, 2025 11:14 pm</p><hr />
